{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sports and Leisure", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Mountain Climbing", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " When to Use -ed and -ing Adjectives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Adjectives which are formed from Infinitive verb forms can have two types of endings: <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> and <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span>.<br/> Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> describe how someone feels.<br/> Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> describe how something or someone is, or how a situation makes someone feel.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> can only be used to describe feelings or emotions. They describe how a person feels. They cannot be used to describe an object or situation.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">Sir Edmund Hillary was <span class=\"strong\">fascinated</span> by the idea of climbing Mt. Everest.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> can be used either with a person or a situation. They describe the characteristics of a person or a situation. They also describe how a situation makes you feel. <br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">Sir Edmund Hillary found the idea of climbing Mt. Everest <span class=\"strong\">fascinating</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare the differences:<br/> <ul><li>Sir Hillary is <span class=\"strong\">fascinated</span>. (He feels fascinated.)<br/> <li>Sir Hillary is <span class=\"strong\">fascinating</span>. (He is a fascinating person.)<br/> <li>Climbing Mt. Everest is a <span class=\"strong\">fascinating</span> challenge. (It causes people to feel fascinated.)</ul> You cannot say <span class=\"italic\">Mt. Everest is fascinated</span>, since it is not a person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is very easy to become <span class=\"strong\">frustrated</span> if progress is slow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Because it is such a <span class=\"strong\">frustrating</span> activity, climbers must be resourceful.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past Passive to Report Events", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice </span>when you want to report events that happened in the past in a general way.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Most of spoken English uses active speech. When you use an active sentence to report an event, the subject is the focus of the sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Journalists (subject)  <span class=\"strong\">reported</span> a sharp increase in mountain climbing as a recreational activity (object). </li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">passive sentence</span> puts the emphasis on the object of the active sentence. When you use a passive sentence to report an event, the object of the active sentence now becomes the subject and focus of the passive sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>A sharp increase in mountain climbing as a recreational activity (subject) <span class=\"strong\">was reported by</span> many journalists (object).</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past passive</span> form to report events in an impersonal way. The subject is not specific, but general.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li><span class=\"strong\">It was said</span> that mountain climbing <span class=\"strong\">was only practiced by</span> seasoned explorers, but that has changed over the years.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"strong\">be</span> verb followed by the <span class=\"strong\">past participle</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the structure:<br/> subject + Simple Past passive reporting verb + To-Infinitive (Perfect or Perfect Continuous tense)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It was thought to be too high, dangerous, and terrifying to climb.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was later confirmed that the New Zealander had been the first to set foot at the top.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was a New Zealander and a Nepali sherpa who were credited with first reaching the peak.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For many years, Hillary and Norgay were reported to have summited together.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to achieve ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to succeed in accomplishing a goal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Clinton Thomas Dent was convinced that it could be achieved.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about mountain climbing.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feat", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a difficult challenge", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The feat wouldn't be successfully accomplished, however, for another 50-plus years. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "expedition ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an organized trip or adventure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After several failed expeditions, it was Edmund Hillary who was credited with first reaching the peak.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sherpa", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a Himalayan mountain guide", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tenzing Norgay was a Nepali sherpa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "well-equipped", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having the appropriate equipment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Alpinists must be well-equipped.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "equipment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They must have the appropriate gear, like ropes and pitons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "piton", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a spike that is driven into rock to aid in climbing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The climber drove the piton into the rock.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to summit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reach the top of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For thrill-seekers, the rush of summiting outweighs the fear.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ascent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of climbing or moving towards the top of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Each mountain ascent presents new challenges.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "steep", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a slope that has a sharp angle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If the mountain is steep and icy, climbers have to take extra precaution.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob05aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and research four famous firsts (e.g. First person to climb Everest).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fold a piece of paper in half to create four panels.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a headline for each of the famous achievements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short paragraph detailing each one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your \u201cbook of records\u201d to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research past accomplishments.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write headlines about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a short informational paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my results with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about sports and leisure time.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, 