rect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le02ob05re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 0}], "id": 0}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn10le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "For most of modern history, Mount Everest was said to be unclimbable. At 8,848 meters, it was thought to be too high, dangerous, and terrifying to climb.  It was first suggested to be possible in 1885 in a book entitled <span class=\"italic\">Above the Snow Line</span>. The author, Clinton Thomas Dent, was convinced that it could be achieved. The feat wouldn't be successfully accomplished, however, for another 50-plus years. <br/>After several failed expeditions, it was a New Zealander, Edmund Hillary, and a Nepali sherpa, Tenzing Norgay, who were credited with first reaching the peak.<br/>For many years, Hillary and Norgay were reported to have summited together, but it was later confirmed that the New Zealander had been the first to set foot at the top."}, {"time": "54700", "image": "engenn10le02ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Mountain climbing used to be an activity only done by explorers like Hillary and Norgay, but over time it has become a mainstream sport. That being said, this challenging sport is certainly not for the timid or careless. To be a successful mountaineer, a person needs to be patient. It is very easy to become frustrated if progress is slow or weather conditions force a change of plan.<br/>Because it is such a frustrating activity, climbers must be resourceful. They must use their brains as well as their bodies to reach the top of the mountain. Lastly, alpinists must be well-equipped with the appropriate gear, including ropes and pitons."}, {"time": "98000", "image": "engenn10le02ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Each mountain ascent presents new challenges and a climber has to be prepared for different mountain conditions and environmental factors. If the mountain is steep and icy, climbers have to take extra precaution. They must plan their climbs well and calculate each step.\nMountain climbing, like most exciting sports, can be dangerous. But for thrill-seekers, the rush of summiting outweighs the fear."}]}}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "id": 0}]}